+# dsh-llm-glm-normalize
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+A dependency-light **stream folding** library for a known GLM OpenAI-Responses gateway quirk: the gateway may open a short text block, then emit a later text block containing the complete answer. Without normalization an assembler would retain the short prefix AND the complete answer as two visible blocks. The fold rewrites the later block's end onto the earlier index so only the complete text survives.
+
+The fold operates on a **structural** subset of assistant events: it reads only `type`, `contentIndex`, `delta`, and `content`, and passes every other event through unchanged. Any pi-ai-shaped event stream — or a structural twin from another provider — can be normalized without importing pi-ai. `glmTextFold` is a composable `StreamEventNormalizer` and composes through `chainStreamNormalizers`, so a stream translator can chain provider quirks without owning their implementations.
+
+It is a **library, not a service or plugin**: no `ctx`, registers nothing, emits no events. The pi-ai adapter (`dsh-llm-pi-ai`) applies the fold for its `glm` provider route and re-exports the seam.
+
+## API
+
+```ts ignore-check
+import {
+  glmTextFold,
+  normalizeGlmTextEvents,
+  chainStreamNormalizers,
+} from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-glm-normalize'
+import type { StreamEventNormalizer } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-glm-normalize'
+```
+
+| Export | Role |
+|---|---|
+| `normalizeGlmTextEvents(events)` | The fold as an async generator: rewrites a folded `text_end` onto the earlier index, passes everything else through. |
+| `glmTextFold(events)` | The fold as a `StreamEventNormalizer` for composition. |
+| `chainStreamNormalizers(...normalizers)` | Composes normalizers in argument order into one; zero arguments is the identity transform. |
+| `StreamEventNormalizer<E>` | The seam type: `(events: AsyncIterable<E>) => AsyncIterable<E>` for `E extends { type: string }`. |
+
+## When the fold applies
+
+A `text_end` folds onto an earlier unclosed block when:
+
+- the later block's content starts with the earlier accumulated text; or
+- the earlier accumulated text is at most 16 characters and the later content is at least 64 characters (a long replay of a stub the gateway truncated).
+
+A later text block opened before the earlier one closes is held until its `text_end` decides, so tool-call and thinking block order stay unchanged. Pending text ends flush before any tool-call or thinking block, and again at end of stream.
+
+## Model Experience
+
+None, as this package is a pure event-stream normalization utility that registers no model context.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+No KV-cache effect: the fold only rewrites assistant text-block indexes; token counts and request caching are decided by the model adapter and the request itself.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- **pi-ai-shaped events only** — the fold reads a structural subset of assistant events; a provider with a different event vocabulary needs its own normalizer composed through `chainStreamNormalizers`.
+- **Content matching is heuristic** — the length rule decides a genuinely distinct short block that shares a prefix with a stub; a gateway that stops replaying complete text leaves both blocks visible.
